[ ] Move calendar-sync policy from the filesystem adapter into Core =calendar-sync-into-core $filesystem/calendar.rs parses ICS and decides linking, migration matching and link cardinality before calling Core prepare_sync. Three layers: Plan domain owns link invariants; Core ICS/sync owns codec, UID evidence, roll-forward; adapter reads bytes and delivers effects. Needs a charter; the user drafts the outcome. Claim c41. After plan-link-sidecar-only.$ !2 ^2026-09-24T11:22 #01a0d4a7-f0bd-7465-8583-757b4b3e7dc1
[ ] Unify the three charter-stem derivations =unify-charter-stem $Core action_files.rs, nvim init.lua and cli/plan.rs disagree, e.g. on charters/next.actions and README.md. Keep one definition plus a shared conformance fixture that the Lua copy also tests against. Claim c42.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T11:22 #01a0d4a7-f0c4-775b-adcb-b7f6402d7e43
[ ] Refuse ambiguous title matches when archiving a charter $select_archive_charter in filesystem/archive_charter.rs falls back to a partial title match that silently takes the first hit; it should error on more than one, as ambiguous UUID prefixes already do.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T11:22 #01a0d4a7-f0cc-74ef-86bb-27e5d766535f
[ ] Pass the clock into Core instead of reading it $domain/update.rs sets completed_at from Local::now; archive_actions.rs plan_action_archive wraps it the same way. transaction.rs already takes now as a parameter, so follow that.$ !4 ^2026-09-24T11:22 #01a0d4a7-f0d4-7166-8093-108e47d82f57
[ ] Remove the mutations.rs re-export shim $Durable-verbs charter closed 2026-08-15 but cli/charter.rs still imports CharterUpdate via clearhead_cli::mutations. Import from clearhead_core and delete the module. Also fix the misplaced Count-the-actions doc comment on crystallized_sidecar.$ !5 ^2026-09-24T11:22 #01a0d4a7-f0db-716e-91d0-4047bd3a2b33
[ ] Resolve one calendar sync conflict at a time =sync-conflict-per-action $sync calendar --conflict action or calendar resolves every conflict at once. Add a per-action scope so doctor can name one precise resolution command per conflict. Needed by sync-conflicts-in-doctor.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T22:47 #01a0d71a-8891-72dc-b47c-341c025d3b2f
[ ] Report unresolved calendar sync conflicts in doctor =sync-conflicts-in-doctor $DECIDED 2026-09-24: doctor is the persistent view of workspace state. Warn per unresolved conflict with action, field and both values, plus the exact per-action resolution command. Never auto-fix: choosing a side is judgement. Transport health such as vdirsyncer stays out of ClearHead; staleness detection belongs to the scheduler.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T22:47 #01a0d71a-889a-73d3-aea7-d9720a0bb051
[ ] Rewrite the Radicale and vdirsyncer cookbook for unattended service =cookbook-unattended-sync $docs/cookbook/radicale-vdirsyncer.md teaches the three patterns that silently stopped the user's sync for two months: pass for an unattended service, where the gpg-agent cache caps at 24h; one chained oneshot where a transport failure also stops clearhead sync; and OnUnitActiveSec timers, which can end up never scheduled. Its conflict-hiding rationale for chaining is also wrong, since sync exits 0 on conflicts. Document the working setup: a systemd-creds credential decrypted by the vdirsyncer password.fetch command, separate clearhead-sync and vdirsyncer units on staggered OnCalendar timers, and OnFailure hooks.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T22:47 #01a0d71a-88a1-7319-b7f2-0b7964cfb13a
